WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.400
What if you parallel park using a different method, pointing your car toward the curb at an angle,

00:05.620 --> 00:09.660
reversing straight back, and putting on full lock at the very last minute?

00:10.320 --> 00:13.440
Blackburn's geometry still tells you the best angle of approach.

00:13.920 --> 00:17.480
You apply full lock right as corner A passes point G,

00:17.840 --> 00:20.780
placing your car onto the exact same turning circle.

00:21.280 --> 00:26.020
The ideal angle of approach is simply the angle a tangent to the circle at G

00:26.020 --> 00:29.300
makes with the curb, minus the tangent angle at A.

